Z||000000||reddog||10-12-2001||08:08 PM||||I just got my 17" wheels and tires on my 86 GT but there still is too much space in the fender wells. What is the best way to lower my GT and can anyone recommend any particular brands or products?||||reg||5
Z||000001||qwikgta||10-12-2001||11:00 PM||||There is a set of dropped spindles on Ebay now, price is (was) $250.  Also, I think many companies still offer lowering springs for the 84-87.  I (88) on the other hand just cut my coils for about a 1.5 inch drop.  Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||G-Nasty||10-13-2001||02:34 AM||||I have suspension techniques front and rear lowering springs on my 87 gt- I got 16" front and 17" rear O.Z. corsa rims. I have bel-tec 2" drop spindles in front. The car sits too low in front but looks kik ass- I need to get a digital pic of my ride...<BR>$79.oo bux for fr and 79 for rear coils (jc whitney)Spindles will be hard to find now days. If you get fierostore brake upgrade that uses beretta spindles...your tires will stick out about a 1/4+ inch and will eat your fenders. I need to cut rear coils bout an inch for the perfect ride. I have Konis up front and bilsteins in back||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-13-2001||04:02 AM||||Setup I'm using is 2" Street Dreams drop spindles for the front (same as ones on Ebay) and 1 to 1-1/2" Suspension Techniques drop springs (JCWhitney) for rear.<P>It has a slight rake, but I'm ok with it for now.<P><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Banzai||10-13-2001||12:39 PM||||I just picked up a set of Eibach springs (Pro-Kit, 1" drop) from shox.com for 219 shipped.  The S/T lowering springs are on backorder for at least two months.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dgzfiero||10-13-2001||08:07 PM|||| Banzai   I put those springs on my 88. Unfortunately you need a ruler to tell the difference. It was only about a 1/2" in the front and maybe 3/4" in the back. It did make it ride a little better then the old wore out factory ones though. You really couldn't tell the difference.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dgzfiero||10-13-2001||08:20 PM|||| Oops, its the prokit ones I put on||||reg||1
